hi everyone i'm alana and today i am  playing borderlands the pre-sequel at a  preview event here in sydney  borderlands the pre-sequel is a game  that is set between borderlands 1 and 2  so instead of going with borderlands 1.5  they made up their own word because why  not  similar to the others is a first-person  shooter with a bunch of fancy rpg  elements and it really supports co-op  gameplay with the four playable  characters all of whom have existed in  previous games  there's athena claptrap nisha and  wilhelm and i went with wilhelm  so the pre-sequel is set on pandora's  moon and follows the story of handsome  jack from borderlands 2 becoming a  villain but also apparently becoming  handsome because they just refer to him  as jack in this one  you actually start off as one of jack's  henchmen but it's not so bad because he  starts off as a much nicer guy still  kind of arrogant and cheeky and weirdly  lovable but he has some good intentions  and the game follows what went so  horribly wrong to make him an evil  maniac  more importantly though because it's set  on the moon it plays like a super lasery  spacey sci-fi concoction with oxygen  tanks and low gravity environments  this means you get to bounce around  areas shooting glowy lasers at weird  space enemies and it's ridiculous but  awesome there are also freeze weapons  which i found particularly cool which  you can freeze enemies and make them  shatter before you  oxygen tanks are slightly less awesome  because you're in space you can run out  of oxygen  you have to pick up oxygen tanks and  enemies drop or enter a room that might  refill you completely it adds an extra  thing to think about but not one that is  really exciting or really adds to the  gameplay  it's almost just a minor inconvenience  another thing that ought to be mentioned  is claptrap's special ability type thing  which if activated will affect the  entire party  an example of it is that everyone  playing won't be able to stop shooting  if he activates it even if there are no  enemies around meaning you just  basically waste all of your ammo  speaking of funny though the dialogue is  fantastic i had issues with previous  borderlands games being super fetch  questy and it just feels like oh yeah do  this go here do this without a whole lot  of motivation  and while the new one still feels the  same in mission design it's like they've  paid even more attention to having  brilliantly scripted side characters  even ones you might never meet again to  make things consistently amusing no  matter what you're doing  heaps of them are australian too with  actual australian voice actors which is  awesome  borderlands the pre-sequel is set to  release on the 14th of october and is  coming to the xbox 360 ps3 and pc  it's not coming to next-gen consoles at  this point but it may eventually  i guess my initial impression here is  that it's very similar to previous games  it feels much  much more creative and definitely much  more australian which is a nice and  unique touch
 

